A||||1||ChadMan||Tie-rod ends...some sucess...some terror||||11||
Z||000000||ChadMan||09-10-2001||03:13 PM||||Try as I might, I could not get the inner tie-rod ends off my 88 Coupe.  There's very little room to swing a wrench in there...and I didn't want to take the steering rack off.<P>So I put the new outer tie-rod ends on (piece of cake), aligned the thing the best I could, and went to the Grandview Tuffy (trustworthy thus far) to get an estimate to install my inners.  At first they were reluctuant to install my parts, but after I showed the manager the Dickman tie-rod ends, he seemed reassured and quoted me $200 including alignment.  I thought that sounded fair.<P>So Wednesday, my Fiero goes under a stranger's wrench.  That is always a terrifying feeling...<P>Please wish me luck and pray for the safe and inexpensive return of my Coupe.||||reg||11
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||09-10-2001||03:35 PM||||Good luck to you.  Alignment time is always my worst fear.||||reg||1
